---
layout: base.njk
permalink: /work/
title: All work
description: Case studies in AI-driven product design, service design and design systems.
---
{% from "partials/work-card.njk" import card %}
{% from "partials/icons.njk" import chevron, checkCircle %}

{#- "Back" is a pill with a leading chevron, in its own 83px band between the nav
    and the content (Figma 2227:8101 / 2227:8102) — not a plain text link. -#}
<div class="back-row">
  <div class="container">
    <a class="pill-link" href="/">{{ chevron("left") }} Back</a>
  </div>
</div>

<section class="container section section--tight" aria-labelledby="all-work-heading">
  <h1 class="section-title" id="all-work-heading">All work</h1>

  {#- Filter chips (Figma 2227:8110). Counts come from the `topics` collection, so
      they are always correct — there is no hand-maintained list to fall out of
      sync. The active chip keeps the same background and marks itself with a tick
      plus bold ink text, rather than inverting to a dark fill. -#}
  <div class="filter-bar" data-filter role="group" aria-label="Filter work by topic">
    <button class="chip chip--button" type="button" data-filter-all aria-pressed="true">
      <span class="chip__tick">{{ checkCircle() }}</span>
      All ({{ collections.caseStudies | length }})
    </button>
    {%- for topic in collections.topics %}
    <button class="chip chip--button" type="button"
            data-filter-topic="{{ topic.name | slugifyTopic }}" aria-pressed="false">
      <span class="chip__tick">{{ checkCircle() }}</span>
      {{ topic.name }} ({{ topic.count }})
    </button>
    {%- endfor %}
  </div>

  <p class="filter-empty" hidden data-filter-empty>No case studies match that filter.</p>

  <ul class="work-list" data-filter-list>
    {%- for item in collections.caseStudies %}
    <li class="work-item" data-topics="{% for topic in item.data.topics %}{{ topic | slugifyTopic }}{% if not loop.last %} {% endif %}{% endfor %}">
      {{ card(item, "h2", "time") }}
    </li>
    {%- endfor %}
  </ul>
</section>
